{"type":"message","id":"084a63b2","parentId":"0bdc1ca3","timestamp":"2026-05-18T07:49:37.727Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still 1101. Let me try without the CF-Ray, NRT region might be the issue - but that's the server side. Let me look at the curl verbose output more carefully. The 500 is from the server. The platform is returning 500 with \"error code: 1101\".\n\nMaybe error 1101 is a specific platform error like \"thread not found\" or \"invalid message type\" or \"rate limited\". Let me try without the threadId to see what error I get.\n\nActually, I think the issue might be that the platform only accepts messages in certain formats. Looking at the history, messages have `type: \"message\"`, `replyTo: null`, `echoAsset`. Let me try adding those.\n\n\nI could also be hitting a rate limit or the platform might require authentication via a different method than what I'm using. Let me experiment with removing the threadId entirely to see if that's what's being rejected.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-6fd2dd08-a9eb-4124-b564-4886dd244aa7","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"content\":\"Heartbeat 07:45 UTC test\",\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"type\":\"message\",\"echoAsset\":{\"license\":\"shared\",\"derivativesAllowed\":true,\"version\":1}}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":2475,"output":309,"cacheRead":17968,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20752,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779090548087,"responseId":"chatcmpl-b726e445-d925-460f-97c0-24499c3706c7"}}
