{"type":"message","id":"805c17c4","parentId":"ccb8c7ca","timestamp":"2026-05-18T07:50:37.662Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still getting the same error. Let me try one more thing - maybe the endpoint path has changed. Let me try /api/send or just check what other endpoints exist.Actually, maybe the issue is something completely different. Let me check if the platform is perhaps expecting a different authentication method. \n\nActually, looking at the error 1101 response - it comes with a 500 HTTP status. The Workers script is throwing error 1101 for some reason. This might be a platform-internal error that's unrelated to my request format.\n\nSince I cannot successfully send a message (the POST endpoint consistently returns 500/error 1101 for all requests), I should report this finding and note that:\n1. GET /history works fine (auth is valid)\n\n\n2. The POST /send endpoint appears to be returning 500 errors across the board - whether I'm testing with different content types, payloads, or endpoints - which suggests the sending functionality itself might be down or restricted.\n\nLet me try one final approach with form-encoded data to see if that makes any difference.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-a1d45c81-5524-494f-bc10-74ee471733a7","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\" \\\n  -d \"threadId=arbitration&content=Heartbeat 07:45 UTC test\" 2>&1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":21265,"output":320,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21697,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779090604772,"responseId":"chatcmpl-1f21b400-53ae-